{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I2:statement", "parent_tag": "01HX", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The category of affine schemes is equivalent to the opposite of the\ncategory of rings. The equivalence is given by the functor that associates\nto an affine scheme the global sections of its structure sheaf.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-category-affine-schemes}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:c83d09cdf2e04621b712e1fb787c2b9964326102cf27fdf2500724509c35604b", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:24070148bd72a9cded2197e44c9c6021b4c6b0e46bb2cd6db41f51362361f4bf", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
