{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I4:statement", "parent_tag": "01HX", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "The category of affine schemes has finite products, and fibre products.\nIn other words, it has finite limits. Moreover, the products\nand fibre products in the category of affine schemes\nare the same as in the category of locally ringed spaces.\nIn a formula, we have (in the category of locally ringed spaces)\n<MATH_0001>\nand given ring maps <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> we have\n<MATH_0004>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Spec(R) \\times \\Spec(S) =\n\\Spec(R \\otimes_{\\mathbf{Z}} S)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0003": "$R \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\Spec(A) \\times_{\\Spec(R)} \\Spec(B)\n=\n\\Spec(A \\otimes_R B).\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-affine-schemes}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:743575009a2ac154cd26893e02731ede3fe409ec0675d941211e2bfa2dc3882b", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ef6762316628fe31d639a40f057eeea55598ac5c11c204853a3adb30aa5cda83", "source_math_hash": "sha256:61ac93d1ab73bc1c0ae23b3ee137d71605b9505690cf7643cfcac7c0db9448f1"}
